# "{3}{G}{G}: Return this card and target land card from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped." Turn 1 Bot1 plays Fabled Passage and sacrifices it for a Forest, then casts
# Sandman with a Black Lotus; the ability is not offered while Sandman is on the battlefield (the refusal: it works from the graveyard). Turn 2 Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills
# Sandman (a 1/1 with one land). Turn 3, with two Forests and three Moxen, Bot1 activates it from the graveyard (the positive control) with Fabled Passage as the target:
# both return tapped, together, so Sandman is 3/3 (Forest, Forest, Passage). Fabled Passage's own search is not repeated.

